        { name: "Higher Certificate in Court Interpreting", aps: 25, duration: "1 year", description: "Provides formal professional qualification for court interpreters. Equips graduates to render specialised service in court interpreting to the South African legal system, and other spheres such as the medical field, local municipalities, educational institutions, government and business. Admission: NSC pass with Higher Certificate requirement or NCV with appropriate subjects; English HL Level 4 OR English FAL Level 5; at least one other African language at HL Level 4 OR First Additional Language Level 5; APS minimum 25. Mature age applicants with relevant industry experience may be approved by the Registrar. (Source: SPU 2027 Undergraduate Prospectus, p.10, SAQA ID 115460) Jobs: Court Interpreter (R14 000–R55 000/month); Legal Interpreter (R14 000–R55 000/month); Community Interpreter (R12 000–R45 000/month); Conference Interpreter (R18 000–R70 000/month); Health/Medical Interpreter (R14 000–R48 000/month); Government Agency Interpreter (R14 000–R50 000/month).", requirements: [ { subject: "English Home Language OR English First Additional Language", minPercent: 50 }, { subject: "African Language (HL or First Additional Language)", minPercent: 50 } ] },
        { name: "Bachelor of Arts (BA)", aps: 30, duration: "3 years", description: "Develops skilled graduates who can engage critically with the world and apply disciplinary content to resolution of problems. Strong focus on languages (Afrikaans, English, Setswana), History, Heritage Studies, Geography, Mathematics and Sociology. Heritage Studies is a compulsory 1st-year module. Admission: NSC pass with Bachelor's Degree requirements; English HL Level 4 OR English FAL Level 5; Mathematics Level 2 (30–39%) OR Mathematical Literacy Level 3 (40–49%); APS minimum 30. Students wishing to major in Geography require NSC Level 4 (50–59%). A NCV with relevant subjects, or SPU's Higher Certificate in Heritage Studies or Higher Certificate in Court Interpreting, will be considered for entry. (Source: SPU 2027 Undergraduate Prospectus, p.11, SAQA ID 98922) Jobs: Public sector, private sector, NPOs and NGOs — including strategic management, project management, HR management, managerial finance, and business research within lower/middle/senior management (R14 000–R65 000/month depending on role).", requirements: [ { subject: "English Home Language OR English First Additional Language", minPercent: 50 }, { subject: "Mathematics OR Mathematical Literacy", minPercent: 30 } ] }
