        { name: "Diploma in Agriculture", aps: 25, duration: "3 years", description: "Produces students with solid grounding in principles and practices of producing crops and livestock for commercial purposes, primarily under water-stressed regions. Comprehensive introduction to Mixed Farming — graduates emerge as general agriculturalists equipped to become agricultural entrepreneurs or enter postgraduate studies in any sub-discipline of agriculture. Admission: NSC pass with Diploma requirement; English HL Level 4 OR English FAL Level 5; Mathematics Level 3 (40–49%) OR Mathematical Literacy Level 5 (60–69%); Physical Sciences Level 3 (40–49%); Life Sciences Level 3 OR Agricultural Sciences Level 3; APS minimum 25. (Source: SPU 2027 Undergraduate Prospectus, p.12, SAQA ID 120923) Jobs: Agricultural research; Extension farming production; Farmer enterprises; Marketing; Agricultural entrepreneur; Agricultural technician; Farm manager; Agricultural advisor (R14 000–R65 000/month depending on role).", requirements: [ { subject: "English Home Language OR English First Additional Language", minPercent: 50 }, { subject: "Mathematics OR Mathematical Literacy", minPercent: 40 }, { subject: "Physical Sciences", minPercent: 40 }, { subject: "Life Sciences OR Agricultural Sciences", minPercent: 40 } ] },
        { name: "Diploma in Information and Communication Technology (ICT) specialising in Applications Development", aps: 25, duration: "3 years", description: "Career-focused professional qualification featuring industry-referenced knowledge and skills transfer, technological competencies, critical cross-field skills and attitudinal development. Deals with conceptualisation, design, development, implementation and testing of computer software applications. Prepares for careers in Computer Programming and Systems Analysis & Design. Admission: NSC pass with Diploma requirement; English HL Level 4 OR English FAL Level 5; Mathematics Level 3 (40–49%) OR Mathematical Literacy Level 5 (60–69%); APS minimum 25. Highly recommended: Computer Applications Technology (CAT) or Information Technology (IT) as matric subjects. (Source: SPU 2027 Undergraduate Prospectus, p.12–13) Jobs: Software Analyst (R20 000–R80 000/month); Software Application Programmer (R18 000–R75 000/month); Software Application Developer (R22 000–R95 000/month); Web Administrator (R16 000–R60 000/month); Solution Architect (R30 000–R130 000/month); Web Designer (R14 000–R55 000/month); Computer Network Professional (R18 000–R70 000/month); Web Developer (R18 000–R70 000/month); Network Administrator (R16 000–R60 000/month); System Administrator (R18 000–R70 000/month); Network Analyst (R18 000–R68 000/month).", requirements: [ { subject: "English Home Language OR English First Additional Language", minPercent: 50 }, { subject: "Mathematics OR Mathematical Literacy", minPercent: 40 } ] },
        { name: "Advanced Diploma in Information and Communication Technology (ICT) in Applications Development", aps: 0, duration: "1 year", description: "Produces graduates with good theoretical knowledge and practical skills in systems analysis, design and applications development. Deepens professional knowledge, practice and attitudinal skills development; facilitates access to higher-level qualifications such as postgraduate diploma, master's and doctoral studies. Focus on advanced technical skills in Applications Development, core subjects Software Engineering, Development Software, and Project offerings. Admission: Applicants must be in possession of a three-year Diploma in ICT or equivalent at NQF Level 6 within the same field of study; an average of at least 60% in the third-year exit modules. RPL applied per University policy. (Source: SPU 2027 Undergraduate Prospectus, p.13, SAQA ID 111254) Jobs: Senior Software Developer (R28 000–R120 000/month); Systems Architect (R30 000–R130 000/month); Software Engineering Lead (R35 000–R140 000/month); ICT Project Manager (R28 000–R110 000/month); Applications Development Manager (R32 000–R125 000/month).", requirements: [] },
        { name: "Bachelor of Environmental Science", aps: 30, duration: "4 years", description: "Four-year programme equipping students with groundwork in fundamental principles of environmental sustainability, planning and management. Environmental Science examines the dynamic relationships between living organisms, humans, and the abiotic components of the Earth's ecosystems. Core modules include Environmental Management Systems and Remote Sensing and Earth Observation. Students may select electives such as marine ecology, geography, waste management, and sustainability. Admission: NSC pass with Bachelor's Degree requirements; English HL Level 4 OR English FAL Level 5; Mathematics Level 4 (50–59%) — Mathematical Literacy NOT acceptable; Physical Sciences Level 4 (50–59%); Life Sciences Level 4 (50–59%); APS minimum 30. (Source: SPU 2027 Undergraduate Prospectus, p.14, SAQA ID 123429) Jobs: Environmental Scientist (R18 000–R72 000/month); Environmental Consultant (R18 000–R70 000/month); EIA Practitioner (R18 000–R75 000/month); Urban Sustainability Specialist (R20 000–R78 000/month); Rural Resource Planner (R18 000–R70 000/month); Public Health Officer (R22 000–R84 000/month); NGO Researcher (R16 000–R60 000/month); Academic (R25 000–R90 000/month).", requirements: [ { subject: "English Home Language OR English First Additional Language", minPercent: 50 }, { subject: "Mathematics", minPercent: 50 }, { subject: "Physical Sciences", minPercent: 50 }, { subject: "Life Sciences", minPercent: 50 } ] },
        { name: "Bachelor of Science (BSc)", aps: 30, duration: "3 years", description: "Designed to address a critical skills shortage in the country. Produces science graduates with systematic and coherent body of knowledge, understanding of underlying concepts and principles, ability to assess and evaluate scientific information, high level of cognitive and other generic skills, written and spoken communication, computer literacy and competence in applying knowledge through basic research methods and practice. Offered in three sub-field specialisations: Mathematical and Computer Sciences, Physical Sciences and Biological Sciences. Admission: NSC pass with Bachelor's Degree requirements; English HL Level 4 OR English FAL Level 5; Mathematics Level 4 (50–59%) — Mathematical Literacy NOT acceptable; Physical Sciences Level 4; Life Sciences Level 4; APS minimum 30. (Source: SPU 2027 Undergraduate Prospectus, p.14, SAQA ID 97908) Jobs: Biological Sciences — Biologist (R16 000–R65 000/month), Conservation Scientist (R16 000–R60 000/month), Curator (R16 000–R67 000/month), Ecologist (R16 000–R65 000/month), Molecular Biologist (R18 000–R80 000/month). Mathematical and Computer Sciences — Banking (R15 000–R55 000/month), Insurance (R14 000–R50 000/month), Statistician (R22 000–R95 000/month), Computer Programming (R18 000–R75 000/month), Operations Research (R22 000–R85 000/month), Cyber Security Analyst (R22 000–R100 000/month), Forensic Computer Analyst (R20 000–R80 000/month), Software Analyst (R20 000–R80 000/month). Physical Sciences — Physicist (R22 000–R90 000/month), Chemical Analyst (R18 000–R70 000/month), Quality Control (R16 000–R60 000/month), Forensic GIS Analyst (R20 000–R75 000/month), Geographer (R18 000–R70 000/month).", requirements: [ { subject: "English Home Language OR English First Additional Language", minPercent: 50 }, { subject: "Mathematics", minPercent: 50 }, { subject: "Physical Sciences", minPercent: 50 }, { subject: "Life Sciences", minPercent: 50 } ] },
        { name: "Bachelor of Science in Data Science", aps: 30, duration: "3 years", description: "Strong mathematics core focused on data science and applications. Addresses the need for predictive models in diverse disciplines such as clinical research, intelligence, consumer behaviour and risk management. Graduates are employable and eligible for further study in honours or postgraduate diploma studies. Admission: NSC pass with Bachelor's Degree requirements; English HL Level 4 OR English FAL Level 5; Mathematics Level 5 (60–69%) — Mathematical Literacy NOT acceptable; APS minimum 30. (Source: SPU 2027 Undergraduate Prospectus, p.15) Jobs: Data Scientist (R28 000–R120 000/month); Data Architect (R32 000–R130 000/month); Data Analyst (R20 000–R80 000/month); Data/Analytics Manager (R35 000–R140 000/month); Data Engineer (R28 000–R120 000/month); Intelligence Analyst (R22 000–R85 000/month); Data Mining Engineer (R28 000–R115 000/month).", requirements: [ { subject: "English Home Language OR English First Additional Language", minPercent: 50 }, { subject: "Mathematics", minPercent: 60 } ] }
